Full URI leak on trailing-slash or unparseable paths.

The Javadoc says this static helper returns the last path segment, falling back to `location` itself. Two cases break that contract:

1. Trailing slash (`s3://bucket/prefix/`): the instance `objectName()` returns `""`, so the static helper falls back to the raw `location` string.
2. Unparseable URI (malformed scheme): `StoragePath.of()` throws `IllegalArgumentException` and the catch block also returns `location` verbatim.

Both paths embed the full bucket + key in `ExternalSourceExec.nodeString()` / `ExternalRelation.nodeString()` for every user.

Suggested guard:
```java
String name = null;
try {
    name = StoragePath.of(location).objectName();
} catch (IllegalArgumentException ignored) {}
if (name == null || name.isEmpty()) {
    // strip everything up to and including the last '/' without relying on URI parsing
    int slash = location.lastIndexOf('/');
    name = slash >= 0 && slash < location.length() - 1 ? location.substring(slash + 1) : location;
}
return name;
```

